{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he took the calf.</b> Some say that וישרוף is like ויתך באש, but there is no need, for there is a substance that is placed in fire with the gold and it immediately burns and turns black, and it will never again become gold. This is a tested and true thing:" "<b>And he scattered on the face of the water.</b> This is the water of the stream coming down from the mountain, and he commanded that all Israel drink of this water. This was like ומן העפר אשר יהיה בקרקע המשכן יקח הכהן ונתן אל המים (Numbers 5:17). Now the water renewed a sign upon the calf-worshippers in their faces, or their bellies swelled — for otherwise how did the Levites know who the calf-worshippers were? And they already said that they were few whose intention was evil, while the intention of all the rest was for good, according to their reasoning:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:50.755955709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}